.TH HOST-GUARDIAN 1 "2026-07-26" "host-guardian" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
host-guardian \- verify mount identity and shed named units under memory pressure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B host-guardian
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B host-guardian
checks that each declared mountpoint is still backed by the filesystem it is
supposed to be, and stops operator-nominated units when the host is genuinely
out of memory.
.PP
It is deliberately narrow. Memory, CPU, IO, load and filesystem metrics come
from
.BR prometheus\-node\-exporter (1);
restarting a unit that failed is systemd's own
.B Restart=
directive; killing by cgroup pressure is
.BR systemd\-oomd (8).
.B host-guardian
implements only what none of those cover: verifying a mount is still the
filesystem you declared, and shedding a
.I named
unit rather than whichever cgroup happens to be under the most pressure.
.PP
Results are published as a Prometheus textfile for node-exporter to collect, so
.B host-guardian
listens on no socket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Configuration file. Default
.IR /etc/host-guardian/config.json .
.TP
.B \-\-once
Evaluate once, print the metrics to standard output and exit. Does not act.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The configuration could not be read or is invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A command-line argument was not recognised.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/host-guardian/config.json
Configuration. Thresholds, shed units and mount expectations.
.TP
.I /var/lib/host-guardian/textfile/host-guardian.prom
Prometheus textfile output.
.TP
.I /var/log/host-guardian/incidents
One JSON record when a condition first crosses its sample gate, and one per
action actually taken. A condition that persists is not re-recorded, and a
suppressed action is not recorded at all \- those are visible in
.IR host_guardian_actions_in_window .
Aged out after 30 days by
.IR /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/host-guardian.conf .
.SH SAFETY
An emergency requires both low available memory
.I and
high full memory PSI; either alone is normal. Conditions must persist for
.I consecutive_samples
evaluations before anything acts. Actions are rate limited by a per-unit
cooldown and a global budget per rolling window.
.PP
There is no unlink, prune, reboot or arbitrary-PID kill in the binary. The only
mutation available is
.B systemctl stop
on a unit named in the configuration, and unit names are validated so a
configuration file cannot become arbitrary root execution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd\-oomd (8),
.BR tmpfiles.d (5),
.BR proc (5)
.PP
https://github.com/developerinlondon/host-guardian
